Requirements
Diploma/Degree in any field with 5 years’ working experience as a PRO in the construction industry.
Location
East area

The Senior Conference Producer / Senior Conference Marketing Specialist is a full-time position based in Singapore. As a Senior Conference Producer / Senior Conference Marketing Specialist, you will play a key role as the driving force behind academic conferences. You will gain hands-on experience in all aspects of conference management from concept to execution, with specific responsibilities depending on the type of event. You can let us know your preference during the interview for Senior Conference Producer or Senior Conference Marketing Specialist role.
For virtual conferences, you will be responsible for overseeing both the production and marketing aspects, ensuring seamless execution and maximum engagement throughout the event.
For in-person conferences, you will be responsible for either production or marketing, though your role may extend beyond these areas as additional tasks arise, depending on the needs of the event.
You will be responsible for the following areas:
Production
- Market Research: Conduct in-depth research on market trends, competitor landscapes, and industry challenges;
- Value proposition Creation: Discuss valid topics with the chair and write and delivering event briefs for the marketing and editorial teams;
- Conference agenda curation: Coordinate with chair and session chairs to select the oral and poster presentation candidates, schedule the presentation timing for all slots;
- Stakeholder Engagement: Establish relationships with key stakeholders, including chair, session chairs, speakers to create advocacy for our events;
- Website Management: Keep event websites updated with the latest information, speakers, partners, and sessions;
- Budget Preparation and Tracking: Prepare budget forecast before the event, and update the budget regularly to check the potential profit and loss;
- Customer Service: Provide exceptional service to partners, speakers, and stakeholders, resolving issues promptly;
- Milestone Tracking: Monitor and track progress to ensure KPIs and event targets are achieved;
- Team Coordination: Coordinate with editorial team, marketing team, live session teams;
- Editorial progress monitor: Work closely with the editorial team on abstract processing and with production teams on abstract book preparation;
- Oversee live streaming of virtual events to ensure the smooth operation of the live sessions;
- Onsite Delivery: Lead the creation and delivery of event briefs for on-site delivery, ensuring exceptional on-site execution of the conferences to meet customer expectations;
Marketing
- Marketing strategy creation: Ensure maximum outreach to target markets and promote the conference through various channels
- Conference collateral materials creation: draft copies for brochures, banners, sponsorship prospectus
- Marketing Copywriting: Create promotional copy for marketing channels, including Email campaigns, SM posts, Media partners and editorial needs.
- SEO marketing: Improve the website ranking and increase the website traffic;
- Sponsorship marketing: Secure partners and coordinate their participation and sponsorship;
- Content Development: Create content for conference sessions, interviews, and speaker/host scripts by collaborating with internal and external stakeholders;
- Marketing campaigns progress tracking: Monitor and track progress to ensure the timely execution of all marketing schedules;
- Post-Event Analysis: Conduct evaluations and prepare detailed reports highlighting event outcomes.
Others
- Recognize work processes and/or outcomes that are negatively impacting the project; owns the issue and takes action to address deficiencies by identifying resolutions and notifying the appropriate manager.
Requirements:
- A Bachelor or Master's degree in any subject;
- Candidates with at least 2 years of relevant experience are welcome to apply
- Experience in conference industry is preferred
- Are curious about people and love to speak, build and nurture relations;
- Capable of handling multiple projects, and articulate common objectives for the teams to follow.
- Excellent online call etiquette and written communication skills
- International travel and confidence in face-to-face networking
- Proven ability to work well in a team but also initiative to work on your own
What We Offer:
- Professional and personal development
- International work environment
- Flexible working hours in the limits of a full-time job
- Trips to the other MDPI offices
- Attending Scientific Conferences
- Competitive salary, benefits
A pioneer in scholarly open access publishing, MDPI has supported academic communities since 1996. Our mission is to foster open scientific exchange in all forms, across all disciplines. We operate more than 400 diverse, peer-reviewed, open access journals supported by over 66,000 academic editors. We serve scholars from around the world to ensure the latest research is openly and broadly available.
MDPI is headquartered in Switzerland with additional offices in Europe, Asia and North America. We are committed to ensuring that high quality research is made available as quickly as possible. We also support sustainability projects, with sustainability as a key theme in many journals and through the MDPI Sustainability Foundation.

[What the role is]
Enterprise Singapore is the government agency championing enterprise development. The agency works with committed companies to build capabilities, innovate and internationalise. It also supports the growth of Singapore as a hub for global trading and startups, and builds trust in Singapore’s products and services through quality and standards.
The Partners Division within Enterprise Singapore develops programmes and platforms with partner organisations such as SME Centres and Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) through which EnterpriseSG assists SMEs at scale.
[What you will be working on]
As a Member Of The SMEC Team In The Partners Division, You Will Be Working With SME Centres And IHLs To Assist SMEs In Singapore. The Team Formulates And Implements Strategies Through Which SMECs And IHLs To Support The Growth And Capability Development Of Local SMEs. In Addition, The Team Will Manage The SMEC Centre Programme As Well As EnterpriseSG’s Flagship Programme For Broadbased Companies, Enterprise Leadership For Transformation (ELT) Programme. You Will Be Expected To
- Serve as the primary account manager for SMECs, developing deep understanding of their operational needs, constraints, and required support;
- Strategise, plan and manage projects in partnership with SMECs and IHLs, establishing clear milestones and key performance indicators (KPIs), while ensuring comprehensive tracking and timely reporting of project outcomes;
- Create, manage and review programmes including SME Centre and ELT programmes (operated through SME Centres and IHLs);
- Provide timely reporting of programme feedback and management of data, which includes SMECs and IHLs’ deliverables and fund disbursements;
- Assess and monitor the impact and effectiveness of programmes of both qualitative and quantitative data;
- Work closely with key partners (e.g. TACs, other government agencies) in identifying industry and SME challenges and support the development of relevant projects; and
- Support strategic communications and engagement efforts with SMECs and IHLs.
You will have the opportunity to work closely with business leaders in Singapore.
[What we are looking for]
An ideal candidate would be action-oriented, possess strong stakeholder management skills, and have excellent oral and written communication skills. Candidates with experience in strategy development, programme development and partners management will have an advantage.

Requirements:
At least 1 to 3 years' legal experience gained within a top-tier firm;
Qualified in Singapore;
Strong experience in M&A transactions;
Keen sense of curiosity and adaptability to turn your hands at novel transactions and issues;
Excellent technical and drafting skills coupled with commercial nous;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills (including drafting) and excellent organisational skills.
Ability to work autonomously and effectively manage multiple and often competing priorities;
Build team morale and motivate team members, contributing to the creation of a positive work environment and to assist with training and development;
Lateral thinker to develop innovative solutions to issues that arise during transactions; and
A proactive, positive and energetic approach with a commitment to providing excellent service and, a desire to interact with the market and build client relationships.
Background checks
In order to comply with regulatory and client requirements, Ashurst Perkins Coie will undertake appropriate vetting of staff. When applicants accept a job offer, Ashurst Perkins Coie, alongside a specialist provider, will undertake professional verification and background checks. These checks are only undertaken with consent, and in accordance with our legal and regulatory obligations.
Notice for Recruitment Agencies
Ashurst Perkins Coie is the global law firm for the future economy.
With more than 3,500 client-facing practitioners across 52 offices worldwide, we advise a broad range of clients, and have a distinct strength in technology, energy & infrastructure, and financial services – three sectors at the forefront of economic transformation.
Combining global scale, sector insight, and technological capability, Ashurst Perkins Coie helps clients unlock opportunity with market-leading experience in complex transactions, litigation, and regulatory matters.
We support clients through a shifting landscape where technology, and AI in particular, is both an accelerator and disruptor to their business opportunities and challenges and is reshaping how energy, data, and capital move across markets.
Our strengths have earned our lawyers recognition across the profession, and more importantly, the trust of our clients. Our people are our greatest asset, advising clients on complex, cross-border matters and collaborating seamlessly across markets and practices. We offer a global platform for career-defining work and an opportunity to help shape a firm with the culture and confidence to compete at the highest level.
For Ashurst Perkins Coie, innovation is our tradition. We have a long legacy of helping clients through moments of transformation with the insight to help them stay ahead.
Our Singapore team provides local knowhow across multiple practices, including banking and finance, corporate M&A, as well as complex arbitration and civil litigation on a wide range of areas. Through the formal alliance, Ashurst Perkins Coie ADTLaw offers clients an integrated international service, with clients benefiting from innovative global insights and locally tailored advice.
To find out more please visit our website

