Description:
Job Purpose:
Partner Account Manager (PAM) represents Kaspersky Lab to the Channel, communicates the strategy and vision. For Kaspersky Lab Partners, PAM serves as main point of entry for any business-related questions, and advocates the partner within Kaspersky Lab.
This role is partner-facing with the core accountability of landing renewal sales through Managed Partners portfolio, develops New Business and recruits new Managed Partners.
Main responsibilities:
Partners Relationships Management
• Work with assigned portfolio of Managed partners to ensure revenue targets are met;
• Partners Joint Business planning and plan execution, maintain established Rhythm of Business (QBR, MBR, and others);
• Serve as main point of entry for any business-related questions and needs, be a trusted adviser for all levels and roles in Partner;
• Align partners strategy with region sales and development strategy;
• Perform Partners management in a compliant way, follow the channel rules of engagement, make sure Partners comply with Kaspersky Lab business policies;
• Help to connect Kaspersky Lab partner community and Kaspersky Lab Area level to drive partner satisfaction;
• Advocate the partner within Kaspersky Lab;
Partners Performance Management
• Drive New Business development and find New Managed Partners to work with;
• Maintain renewals rate target;
• Execute on Partners Enablement and Growth engines;
• Drive upsell/cross-sell opportunities in assigned Managed Partners portfolio;
• Participate in trainings and readiness sessions to be able to pitch to Managed Partners new products, product features, licensing, sales skills, partner program and other KL programs;
• Makes Managed Partners utilize every Partner program feature: Deal Registrations, Incentives, Rebates, Leads transfer, etc.;
• Review SMB and mid-market customer opportunities and use all available resources to accelerate deal closure;
• Manage Partners participation in KL marketing programs and help to land marketing activities, collaborates with Regional Marketing department;
Enterprise Partners Management
• Work with assigned Enterprise & SI Partners to ensure Enterprise revenue targets are met
• Orchestrated internal resources within Enterprise Team
• Manage and review pipeline of Enterprise partners
• Drives Account planning process
Qualification Requirements
• Minimum 7-10 years of sales experience, preferably in cybersecurity industry, including at least 5 years of experience in partner or channel management;
• Proven track record of achievement against quota;
• Reasonable level of technical proficiency;
• Inclusive and collaborative – driving teamwork and cross-team alignment;
• Strong partner relationship management;
• Strong executive presence including communication and presentation skills with a high degree of comfort to large and small audiences;
• Bachelor’s degree required;
• Experience in working with Security solutions is an advantage;
• SFDC knowledge preferred.

1. Performing Artiste is able to perform in English, Chinese & Vietnamese languages ;
2. Performing Artiste is able to communicate in English , Chinese & Vietnamese with co-workers, staff and Management;
3. Performing Artiste is able to collectively involve in events planning and new choreography as and when required;
4. Performing Artiste is able to work independently as an individual as well as a group.

The Chinese Media Group (CMG) is seeking a highly motivated Performance Marketing & Campaign Specialist to join its Branding & Marketing (B&M) team. The B&M section is responsible for co-developing and implementing respective CMG’s products brands strategies, as well as driving effective marketing and communication plans to create strong brand value; these include Lianhe Zaobao, Shin Min Daily News, ThinkChina, ZBSchools, HeyKaki, UFM100.3 and 96.3 Hao FM etc.
As a Performance Marketing & Campaign Specialist, you will be the subject matter expert in omnichannel marketing efforts, especially in driving digital performances, generating brand awareness and engagement, in not only Singapore, but also Asia and global regions. You are expected to:
- Develop a thorough understanding of CMG and its brands’ mission and business goals;
- Set up campaigns, optimize audience targeting, ad placement and ROI across programmatic, display, social media, SEM, email marketing etc. to increase effectiveness of ads;
- Coordinate closely with internal stakeholders such as branding specialists, regional marketer, lifecycle marketer, designer, social media, ad operations etc. to execute marketing plans of varying scales within budget;
- Research and develop top to mid marketing funnel strategy for CMG brands, using paid digital marketing to amplify and effectively increase market share;
- Derive benchmarks and KPIs, monitor, analyze and report campaign performance to internal and external stakeholders, where applicable;
- Utilize data and insights to recommend opportunities for improvement and guide strategic decisions;
- Support with copywriting and creation of various communication materials, primarily campaign artworks for owned platforms and social media etc.;
- Liaise with internal and external stakeholders for approval of key artwork, communication materials;
- Research and provide industry updates, trends and insights that can help create potential opportunities;
- Provide guidance to internal stakeholders on digital campaign optimization;
- Build and manage relationships with vendors, ad platform partners, and agencies;
- Perform knowledge sharing within the B&M team, as well as within CMG to educate and inform on best practices; and
- Ensure confidentiality of all channel and performance data.
Job Requirements
- Degree/Diploma holder with at least 3 years of related working experience in media, digital marketing or agency;
- Proven experience in developing and executing media placement across various channels (e.g. Google, Meta, TikTok, X, Taboola, Outbrain, Baidu, WeChat etc.) in Singapore and global regions;
- Proven experience in using marketing analytics tools and data visualization tools, including but not limited to GA4, Lookerstudio, Tableau, Excel, Google Sheets etc;
- Proven experience in ad platforms integration with strong working knowledge in API, SDK or event creating on GTM;
- Strong working knowledge of the digital media space with an emphasis in paid social, search, display, video and mobile etc;
- Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and Mandarin, as this role mainly supports Chinese products;
- Able to produce effective presentations, and appreciate compelling content;
- Kept abreast of changes in marketing and content trends, technologies, social media landscape and consumer behaviors;
- Highly proactive, detail-oriented and good at project management; good news sense would be advantageous;
- Able to multitask with tight deadlines in a fast-paced environment;
- Able to work independently but also connect with people and collaborate as a team; and
- Able to work on weekends due to campaigns.

